Skyve Helper Script - TODO List

    Project Status: Active Development (Last Updated: 26 Apr 2026)

📋 Quick Summary

This document tracks the implementation status, known issues, and future work for the Skyve Mod Manager installer script for Cities Skylines II on Linux.
🔴 Critical Issues (Fix Before Release)
1. Typos and Spelling Errors

    Fix "attemt" → "attempt" (welcome message)
    Fix "resposibility" → "responsibility" (header comment)
    Fix "enviroment" → "environment" (welcome message)
    Fix "Cpn-Neemo" → "Con-Neemo" or correct author name
    Fix "saved saves" → "saved games" (welcome message)

2. Incomplete Variable Definitions

    SKYVE_PATH is commented out in first script version
    SKYVE_REL calculation needs validation for edge cases
    Verify EXECUTABLE path construction works with custom Steam directories

3. Error Handling Gaps

    Add timeout handling for protontricks .NET installation (can hang indefinitely)
    Handle case where update-desktop-database fails silently
    Add cleanup on script interruption (Ctrl+C)
    Validate that protontricks-launch command exists before using it

4. Steam Prefix Validation

    Current script checks if $STEAM_ID directory exists but doesn't verify it's a valid Wine prefix
    Should check for drive_c subdirectory specifically
    Add warning if prefix appears corrupted or incomplete

🟡 High Priority Features
1. Dependency Installation

    .NET 4.8 Installation Logic
        Re-implement from first script version with proper error handling
        Add progress indication during installation (it can take several minutes)
        Verify installation succeeded before continuing
        Handle case where user cancels protontricks dialog

    Font Installation
        Research which fonts Skyve requires (currently marked as "may need")
        Add optional font installation step
        Document which fonts are recommended

2. Proton Compatibility Configuration

    Integrate compatibility tool configuration from research notes:

    # Option A: Direct cfg editing
    echo "compat_tool_name=proton_ge_9-12" > "$STEAM_DIR/steamapps/compatdata/$STEAM_ID/compatibilitytool.cfg"

    # Option B: Use steamtinkerlaunch if available
    # Option C: Environment variable override at launch

    Add user choice for Proton version preference
    Document that Steam restart may be required after changes
    Handle Flatpak Steam paths differently

3. User Experience Improvements

    Add "Launch Skyve after installation?" prompt (was in first script, removed in second)
    Add option to skip desktop file creation
    Show installation progress indicators
    Add verbose/debug mode for troubleshooting
    Color-coded output consistency (some sections use colors, others don't)

4. Path Detection Enhancements

    Detect multiple Steam libraries (not just default)
    Handle non-standard Wine prefix locations
    Support for Lutris/GOG installations (not just Steam)
    Better Flatpak Steam path detection (~/.var/app/com.valvesoftware.Steam/)

🟢 Medium Priority Features
1. Logging and Diagnostics

    Add optional log file creation (--verbose flag)
    Include system information in logs (distro, Steam version, Proton version)
    Add diagnostic command to check installation health

2. Update Mechanism

    Check for script updates on startup
    Version tracking in script header
    Changelog display option

3. Uninstall Functionality

    Create companion uninstall script
    Remove desktop file
    Option to remove .NET dependencies (careful not to affect other games)

4. Internationalization

    Support for non-English terminals (UTF-8 handling)
    Consider localization for user prompts

🔵 Low Priority / Nice-to-Have
1. Advanced Features

    Batch installation for multiple users
    Silent/unattended install mode for sysadmins
    Configuration file for persistent preferences
    Integration with mod backup/restore system

2. Documentation

    Add inline code documentation (shellcheck compliant)
    Create FAQ section
    Troubleshooting guide for common errors
    Video tutorial link

3. Testing Infrastructure

    ShellCheck integration in CI/CD
    Automated tests for path detection logic
    Test matrix for different distributions

